The last thing any program in this project does is write here. Specifically, it
writes goodbye.

Nothing has run yet, so this is the placeholder version of that.

What a real goodbye will carry: which session just ended, how long it ran in
ticks and in hours, who was at the table and which scopes they held, the world
hash at the final tick, and where the command log was written. Enough that
somebody reading only this file knows what happened, and can go and watch it.

The world hash matters more than it looks. It is the number that says a replay of
this session will reproduce it -- and if a replay ever ends on a different number,
this file is where the two get compared.

goodbye
